{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"jadegreen-preggers-hapuku","creation_channel":"cli","description":"Scope: `src/rebar/_commands/**`, `_cli/**`, `_engine_support/**`, `_io/**`. ~205 lines leave.\n\nLargest cluster, unanticipated: the bash dispatcher is GONE (no `*.sh`, no `ticket_txn.py`) yet ~16 module docstrings still narrate 'Ports ticket-X.sh', 'byte-parity with the dispatcher arm', 'Tier E cutover', 'until E7'. ~126 lines, confirmed stale rather than merely historical. `docs/bash-migration.md` is the existing home.\n\nVerified stale and confirmed individually: `_commands/txn.py:3-8` cites a shim that does not exist; `_engine_support/reads.py:15-19` states a false reason for the module's location; `_commands/leaf.py:9-12` says tag/untag/archive are 'tracked as child tickets' while all three are defined in that same file; `_engine_support/__init__.py:7-9` cites compat shims that do not exist; `_io/__init__.py:14` says the import side 'lands in a later sub-task' six lines above the line importing it; `_cli/_help.py:3-8` is truncated mid-clause (introduced by 3a53e202a7).\n\n`_engine_support/reads_cli.py` explains the same unknown-option rule in five near-identical blocks — a ->CODE fix (extract one helper) rather than a comment edit.\n\nHeadroom: `_commands/init.py` 799 -> ~782 (18 lines of margin), `_cli/_llm_commands.py` 789 -> ~778 (22) — both WITHOUT any code extraction. The module-size pressure in these two files is partly caused by comments explaining previous module-size splits.\n\nNew ADR proposed: 'Explicit init over silent-implicit tracker creation' — a prior-art survey (git-bug/git-appraise vs git-issue/bugs-everywhere/Fossil) stated in four places.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Every non-KEEP unit in scope is relocated or deleted per its destination\n- [ ] The shard's do_not_move list is appended to `.joe-janitor/tools.md` BEFORE any edit lands\n- [ ] Verified-stale comments are corrected where they document a live invariant, deleted only where obsolete\n- [ ] No load-bearing invariant is lost","id":"4fc1-dbde-6772-401f","parent_id":"373f-8c1d-cef0-41bf","priority":3,"tags":["janitor"],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Comment triage: commands, CLI, engine_support and io"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786047148272816001,"uuid":"65259d30-fb9b-4810-8945-a8ca7e995837"}